{
  "dom_id": "step-e204",
  "name": "Example: Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule",
  "problem": "If $y= x \\arccos x,$ calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the product rule and using the formula for the derivative of $\\arccos x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x) & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x)+\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})+\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
